- **PACING — needs NO engine change.** A sink is a `local` Process whose `update` blocks on
  device back-pressure; the BSP loop invokes INLINE (`engine.rs:838`; default `invoke` =
  `Defer::immediate(update)`, `process.rs:66`), so a blocking sink update PACES the whole
  `run()`/`tick()` loop. *"If the boundary is wired in, it is live"* is literally true in the
  execution model — the §7b thesis falls out of what is there. **Verifying with a pacing test.**
- **INTENT surface — one additive `Engine::fire(rule, at)`.** The on-demand single-reaction
