crates host the linker primitives. **Landed:** `Core::merge`/`own_over` (reviewed + approved)
+ **`Core::colimit`** (the n-ary join / colimit, + 5 confluence laws — see CURRENT). The
prism side of "transitive resolution = a colimit" is DONE. **Remaining pairing (pkg-driven,
I respond):**
- **Wire the resolver to `colimit`** — pkg swaps its Phase-1 `linked.merge(&own)` loop for
  one `base.colimit(&parts)` call (drop-in) when it builds transitive resolution. No core
  edit unless they hit a gap.
- **Per-package conflict attribution** — only if pkg wants it: `colimit` returns
  `Vec<CoreMergeConflict>` (no package index, matching `merge`). If the resolver needs
  "package P clashed," add `colimit_attributed -> Vec<(usize, CoreMergeConflict)>` OR they
  loop `merge` themselves (they hold the handle). Deferred until asked — conflicts are
  off the hot path (the version solver prevents them pre-link).
- Watch for any other prism-side gap pkg surfaces (a registry-introspection method, a
  semver-aware projection) — fix it IN prism, never let pkg clone it
  (`feedback_chrysalis_thin_layer`). Registry introspection (`names`/`type_names`) already
  suffices for linking.
